From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DroidDeck Team <dev@droiddeck.app>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: disable VK_EXT_physical_device_drm on kbase

On Android kbase (/dev/mali0), there are no DRM primary or render nodes
(/dev/dri/card* or /dev/dri/renderD*). Advertising VK_EXT_physical_device_drm
causes compositors like Gamescope to expect valid DRM primary and render
device IDs, failing initialization with "physical device has no primary node".
Follow Turnip's convention (!is_kgsl) by disabling EXT_physical_device_drm
when running over kbase.

---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
index a1b2c3d..e4f5a6b 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
@@ -185,7 +185,7 @@ panvk_per_arch(get_physical_device_extensions)(
       .EXT_non_seamless_cube_map = true,
       .EXT_mutable_descriptor_type = PAN_ARCH >= 9,
       .EXT_multisampled_render_to_single_sampled = true,
-      .EXT_physical_device_drm = true,
+      .EXT_physical_device_drm = !device->kbase_node_path[0],
       .EXT_pipeline_creation_cache_control = true,
       .EXT_pipeline_creation_feedback = true,
       .EXT_pipeline_robustness = true,
